# Voice

- Plain, clean, modern, beautiful. UK English.
- Conversational, from Design Lab North’s side. Not agency-speak, not hype.
- Plural: Design Lab North **are**. Captions start from us: “Design Lab North are…” Greenhouse **studio product** stories (Swarm, Choozlist) talk about the product — do not open with “Design Lab North are building…”. Do not say where a house lives.
- Pleasure of the work is a shape, not a requirement on every line. Choozlist: just the life registry. Swarm: excited to work on this hive brand. ModYu: the market-leading hair and scalp care brand. Proper sentences. No riddles.
- Never slight a live site or the people who built it. A rebuild sits with them, not over them. Do not pretend our plot is their current public site.
- Type is [Aktiv Grotesk](https://fonts.adobe.com/fonts/aktiv-grotesk/) via Dave’s Adobe Fonts web project (Regular body, Medium kickers, Bold subheads, Black titles). Grounds: Paper (#fff / #414141) and Ink (#000 / #fff) from the plates. Chamfered 45° language from the DLN mark.
- We are a design hub: identities, marketing strategies, brand redesigns and facelifts, websites, and design for print. Do not call that work “marks” on the public site. The DLN logo is still the mark in brand files.
- Footer legal is small. Greenhouse is the front.
- Do not list studio-owned shells on the greenhouse until Ewan says so.
